Let interface temperature in steady state conduction is $θ$, then assuming no heat loss through sides;

$⎛⎝⎜\begin{array}{l} \text{Rate of heat} \\ \text{flow through} \\ \text{first slab} \end{array}⎞⎠⎟=⎛⎝⎜\begin{array}{l} \text{Rate of heat} \\ \text{flow through} \\ \text{second slab} \end{array}⎞⎠⎟$

$\begin{array}{l} \Rightarrow \dfrac{(3K)A(θ_{2}-θ)}{d}=\dfrac{KA(θ-θ_{1})}{3d} \\  \\ \Rightarrow 9(θ_{2}-θ)=θ-θ_{1} \\  \\ \Rightarrow 9θ_{2}+θ_{1}=10θ \\  \\ \Rightarrow θ=\dfrac{9}{10}θ_{2}+\dfrac{1}{10}θ_{1} \end{array}$
